# HY578 Lab0: Speech Processing - VUS Discriminator

This project implements a **Voiced/Unvoiced/Silence (VUS) discriminator** for speech signals using time-domain analysis.

## Project Structure

- [Proj0.py](mdc:Proj0.py) - Main implementation of the VUS discriminator
- [H.22.16k.wav](mdc:H.22.16k.wav) - Sample speech waveform (16 kHz)
- [Project0_part1.txt](mdc:Project0_part1.txt) - Lab assignment specification
- [Project 0 Part 1.pdf](mdc:Project 0 Part 1.pdf) - Original lab manual

## Core Algorithm

The VUS discriminator uses two time-domain features:
1. **Short-Time Energy (STE)** - distinguishes voiced (high energy) from unvoiced/silence (low energy)
2. **Zero-Crossing Rate (ZCR)** - distinguishes voiced (low ZCR) from unvoiced (high ZCR)

### Classification Logic
- **Voiced**: High energy AND low ZCR
- **Unvoiced**: Moderate energy AND high ZCR  
- **Silence**: Very low energy (< 0.25 × energy_threshold)

## Key Parameters

- Frame duration: 30 ms (default)
- Frame shift: 10 ms (default)
- Window type: Hamming (default)
- Sample rate: 16 kHz (expected)
- Energy threshold: 0.5 × mean(energy)
- ZCR threshold: 1.5 × mean(ZCR) - 0.3 × std(ZCR)

## Usage

```bash
python Proj0.py --input H.22.16k.wav
```